WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.378
<v Human Services Supervisor>Thanks for making time. I asked to meet because I

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:06.757
<v Human Services Supervisor>keep sending you the hardest county calls, and I realized

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:08.784
<v Human Services Supervisor>I never asked how that lands.

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:12.014
<v Program Consultant>Honestly, I like the counties. I know the lead agency

00:00:12.014 --> 00:00:14.894
<v Program Consultant>staff, and I can usually tell what they mean when

00:00:14.894 --> 00:00:16.046
<v Program Consultant>a call gets heated.

00:00:16.396 --> 00:00:20.063
<v Human Services Supervisor>That shows. I also noticed you have not presented your

00:00:20.063 --> 00:00:22.996
<v Human Services Supervisor>own analysis in two months. Is that connected?

00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:26.389
<v Program Consultant>Probably. After a county meeting I spend the afternoon explaining

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:29.432
<v Program Consultant>what each side meant. By the time I get to

00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:31.866
<v Program Consultant>my own work, the team has moved on.

00:00:32.216 --> 00:00:34.971
<v Human Services Supervisor>So the bridging is real work, and it is eating

00:00:34.971 --> 00:00:37.726
<v Human Services Supervisor>the work you were hired for. Which parts do you

00:00:37.726 --> 00:00:38.552
<v Human Services Supervisor>want to keep?

00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:42.122
<v Program Consultant>The relationships. I would hate to lose those. What I

00:00:42.122 --> 00:00:45.342
<v Program Consultant>do not want is being the only person who can

00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:46.630
<v Program Consultant>explain anything to anyone.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.931
<v Human Services Supervisor>Fair. Here is an idea. Before the next joint meeting,

00:00:50.931 --> 00:00:54.882
<v Human Services Supervisor>I will send written options ahead and build in question

00:00:54.882 --> 00:00:57.252
<v Human Services Supervisor>time, so less clarifying happens afterward.

00:00:57.602 --> 00:01:00.576
<v Program Consultant>That would help. And could two other reviewers start joining

00:01:00.576 --> 00:01:03.551
<v Program Consultant>my county calls? They would learn the contacts, and I

00:01:03.551 --> 00:01:05.930
<v Program Consultant>would not be the single point of failure.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.739
<v Human Services Supervisor>Yes. And I will deliver the hardest message at the

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:13.198
<v Human Services Supervisor>meeting myself. That is my job, not yours. Can I

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:16.656
<v Human Services Supervisor>ask one more thing? Do you ever soften your recommendations

00:01:16.656 --> 00:01:18.040
<v Human Services Supervisor>to keep the peace?

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.416
<v Program Consultant>All the time. I worry that if I am blunt,

00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:24.442
<v Program Consultant>I will be seen as difficult. It is tiring to

00:01:24.442 --> 00:01:25.350
<v Program Consultant>watch every word.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.300
<v Human Services Supervisor>Thank you for saying that. Research on facades at work

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.900
<v Human Services Supervisor>links that kind of constant self-monitoring to exhaustion. I would

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.500
<v Human Services Supervisor>rather hear your real recommendation. What would make that feel

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:36.860
<v Human Services Supervisor>safe?

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:40.635
<v Program Consultant>Knowing you will back the substance if a county pushes

00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:44.061
<v Program Consultant>back. And letting me present the delay analysis myself, start

00:01:44.061 --> 00:01:44.746
<v Program Consultant>to finish.

00:01:45.096 --> 00:01:48.437
<v Human Services Supervisor>Done. I will check in with you after the meeting

00:01:48.437 --> 00:01:51.778
<v Human Services Supervisor>about whether your week actually got lighter. If it did

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.448
<v Human Services Supervisor>not, the plan changes again.
